Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Vowel Four Does Not Change the Note
- Story & Context: At 120 BPM, Sardaana repeats one steady khomus pulse while moving slowly from NARROW to FRONT. Leon keeps the mono bass on one root note and programs a dry electro kick-snare pattern with almost no chord movement. Every time the mouth state reaches FRONT, Maren answers with one clipped suspended-second clavichord dyad. Nyurgun uses woodblock only during NARROW and removes it as the resonance broadens. Midway through, Sardaana enters Cavity Lock on HOLLOW for sixteen bars while Leon changes the kick geometry beneath her. The apparent tonal movement stops even though the machine rhythm becomes more active. Timur enters only when the bass drops out, playing one low tenor subtone under the same khomus fundamental.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Old phonetics chart labeled VOWEL 4 beside one unwavering horizontal pitch line whose spectral bands widen and contract above it, steel khomus reflected in oscilloscope glass, frost at the window edge. Sparse vocal fragments limited to “vowel four,” “same note,” “move the mouth,” and “hold here.”

Track 2: Booth Seven Keeps the Cavity Locked
- Story & Context: At 124 BPM, the track begins with Sardaana frozen in a narrow FRONT resonance while Leon cycles three different electro sequences around the same one-note bass pedal. Maren becomes unusually active, using dead clavichord fifths and octave taps because the khomus spectrum remains fixed. Nyurgun alternates rototom and woodblock as section markers. After two minutes, Sardaana finally opens into a slow HOLLOW-to-OPEN transition; the entire machine arrangement immediately thins to kick, bass, and one snare so the widening formants dominate. A Breath Offset sequence places soft inhalations just before every fourth pluck. The piece ends by snapping back to the original FRONT state with no harmonic cadence.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Acoustic test booth numbered 7 with a mouth cross-section diagram pinned beside the window, several moving sequencer blocks beneath one locked spectral curve, red calibration light glowing above the door. Sparse vocal fragments limited to “booth seven,” “lock the cavity,” “sequence moves,” and “open once.”

Track 3: Transmitter Log Ends on an Open Mouth
- Story & Context: The closer runs at 114 BPM and begins with no hats, no clavichord, and no saxophone. Sardaana plays slow khomus pulses in HOLLOW while Leon uses only kick and a two-note mono-bass figure. Over several minutes the arrangement moves through the full Formant Grid, but each state lasts longer than on the previous tracks. Maren enters only at state boundaries. Nyurgun adds one rototom strike after every Breath Offset. Timur contributes breath-only saxophone attacks during the longest OPEN section. In the final minute, Leon removes the bass and snare, leaving only kick, khomus, and faint room tone. Sardaana opens the mouth cavity to its widest state and stops plucking after one final pulse. The overtone field collapses naturally into silence with no filter sweep or reverb tail added.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Handwritten transmitter log ending with a large open-circle mouth symbol instead of a final frequency number, one last khomus pulse fading across green oscilloscope phosphor, frost and darkness beyond the laboratory window. Sparse vocal fragments limited to “log complete,” “open mouth,” “no filter,” and “leave the tongue still.”

